{"kind":"text","seq":40,"text":"Best banked this round: **excitement 7.70** (up from 7.40 last round), intensity 9.75, nausea 5.27, similarity 0.31 (no penalty).\n\nHow I got there over three tested builds:\n1. Replayed last round's proven 161-piece layout to bank 7.40 immediately.\n2. Added a double-up/double-down small-helix spiral complex in open land south of the layout, with an elevated z144 crossover to close the circuit over my own track — 7.63, and intensity dropped to 9.15.\n3. Used that headroom to re-add a full southern out-and-back airtime run (boosted hops at y20-23) plus an elevated return leg — 7.70 with 19 drops, 130 airtime, 1252m length, 5 inversions.\n\nStopped there since intensity (9.75) is nearly at the 10 ceiling — any added element would likely tip it over and tank the score. No styling done, as instructed.\n\n**Summary: 205-piece steel twister — chain lift into a 31m double-down drop, half-loop + corkscrew, three vertical loops, corkscrew pair, dual helix spirals, and a boosted southern airtime run — excitement 7.70.**"}
